# BUGS

<count> is limited by nothing but its 32 bits, and `fsd` serves one request at a time, so one large `Treadref` or `Twriteref` holds every other client of `fsd` until it is done.

9Px's design gives references other kinds of region, the bytes after the message on TCP and an RDMA key; only the ring transport's VMO exists, so `dref` is local only.
